<title>COLOMBIA: Colombia peso dips 3.2 vs dollar.</title>
<headline>Colombia peso dips 3.2 vs dollar.</headline>
<dateline>BOGOTA 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Colombia's peso fell 3.2 to 1,061.2 pesos against the dollar as multinationals snapped up greenbacks to send abroad.</p>
<p>&quot;There was strong demand from multinationals and from banks looking to build up dollar positions,&quot; one interbank dealer said.</p>
<p>Dealers reported 273 trades worth a total $116.9 million. The peso hit an intraday high of 1,058.2 and sank to a low of 1,064.5.</p>
<p>((--Juan Guillermo Londono, Bogota newsroom, 571 610 7944))</p>
